{"term":"impress","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:0b009bd94cdd1abdda","definition":"To affect (someone) strongly and often favourably; to inspire admiration from (someone).","example":"You impressed me with your command of Urdu.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["make an impression","grab"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:110b7dcb4cda4de1f7","definition":"To mark or stamp (something) using pressure; to apply (something) using pressure.","example":"We impressed our footprints in the wet cement.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["press"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8afd58dd5ccd6d7517","definition":"To transfer or transmit.","example":"The money was impressed into the hands of the financial ministry.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["pass"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:92969ce694f641ca71","definition":"To compel (someone) to serve in a military force.","example":"The press gang used to impress people into the Navy.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["pressgang"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/impress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f3d109711d5e83af0c","definition":"The act of im